SEATTLE PUBLIC SCHOOL DISTRICT - DATA PROCESSING
OPERATOR RUN BOOK - REV 6  MARCH 1983

DAILY
  1. MOUNT SCRATCH TAPE ON MT0: BEFORE 1800.
  2. DISMOUNT THE PUBLIC DISK ONLY AFTER THE LAST
     DIAL-IN LINE HAS CLEARED. CHECK KB34 FIRST.
  3. LOG THE RUN IN THE BOUND BOOK. NOT ON SCRAP.

LINE PRINTER
  A JAM ON THE LP11 USUALLY MEANS THE FORMS TRACTOR
  HAS WALKED. STOP THE QUEUE, CLEAR THE PLATEN, AND
  REALIGN TO THE TOP-OF-FORM MARK. DO NOT RESTART A
  PARTIAL REPORT - REPRINT IT WHOLE.

DIAL-IN
  THE RECORDS PROGRAM IS AVAILABLE TO CLERICAL
  ACCOUNTS ONLY. IF A CLERK REPORTS THEY ARE BEING
  ASKED FOR A PASSWORD TWICE, THE LINE IS NOISY -
  NOT THE PROGRAM. CALL PLANT SERVICE.
